title: '[eth-rpc] Store receipts at index time'

doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    `eth-rpc` stores the receipt and the signed transaction of every transaction it indexes, in
    the same database transaction as the transaction hashes and logs. `eth_getTransactionReceipt`,
    `eth_getBlockReceipts`, `eth_getTransactionByHash`, `eth_getTransactionByBlockHashAndIndex`
    and `eth_getTransactionByBlockNumberAndIndex` are served from the database. A request does
    not fetch the block body and events from the node or make the `eth_receipt_data` and
    `eth_block_hash` runtime calls. Stored receipts are removed with the rest of a block's data
    when the block is pruned from the `eth-rpc` database or replaced by a fork.

    Receipts and signed transactions of blocks in the `eth-rpc` database are served even when the
    node has pruned those blocks.

    On start, `eth-rpc` applies database migration `0005_create_receipts`. It creates the
    `receipts` table and adds a `receipts_version` column to `eth_to_substrate_blocks`. Nothing
    needs to be done by hand. Blocks indexed before the upgrade are not backfilled: their receipts
    are rebuilt from the node on request, as for any block without stored receipts. To store
    receipts for all blocks, index into a new database. The database grows by roughly one JSON
    receipt (without logs) and one RLP encoded transaction per indexed transaction.

    Downgrading to an `eth-rpc` without this migration against the same database fails on start
    with the sqlx migration error `VersionMissing(5)`. Keep a copy of the database from before
    the upgrade, or index into a new database, if a downgrade may be needed.

    `eth-rpc` keeps working with the same runtime versions as before: receipts are built through
    the same runtime calls, once per block when it is indexed.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: patch
